Field What it declares <code>id</code>, <code>version</code> <code>mmm.hierarchical_geo</code>, <code>1.3.0</code>. Specs pick a version with a semver range: <code>use: mmm.hierarchical_geo@^1.3</code> <code>schema_template</code> The input data contract, in canonical names. It can be a function of settings: a template with <code>params</code> such as <code>{group_dim}</code> that are filled from the model's settings <code>settings_schema</code>, <code>fit_schema</code> JSON Schemas of <code>model.settings</code> and <code>model.fit</code>. Every field may carry <code>x-ui-level: basic</code> or <code>advanced</code>; Guided mode shows only <code>basic</code> <code>outputs</code> Output variables with dims and units (<code>units_of: y</code> means "in the target's units") <code>derived</code> Derived quantities, and whether they are cached at fit (<code>cache: fit</code>) or computed on demand <code>plots</code> The plot recipes this model's report shows by default <code>resources</code> Minimum and default resource class, estimated fit time, GPU <p>A schema template with parameters, from a model whose group dim is a setting:</p> <pre><code>params:
  group_dim: {type: string, default: geo}
  time_dim:  {type: string, default: time}
template:
  dims:
    "{group_dim}": {kind: categorical, policy: new_levels, new_level_strategy: pooled}
    "{time_dim}":  {kind: time, policy: extend}
  vars:
    y: {dims: ["{group_dim}", "{time_dim}"], dtype: float64, role: target}
</code></pre>
